[38;2;124;124;124mcolor is always the same (determined by the invariant).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor 2×n with n ≡ 1 mod 3 (n=4, 7): color 2, columns 0, 3, 6, ... (multiples of [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m3, up to n-1).[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mFor 2×n with n ≡ 2 mod 3 (n=2, 5): color 1, columns -1, 2, 5, ... (≡ 2 mod 3, up[0m[38;2;124;124;124mto n-1).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo the reachable columns are spaced 3 apart, at positions ≡ c mod 3 where c is [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mthe color class.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThis means the 2×n strip can be reduced to 1 piece at any position (r, c) where [0m[38;2;124;124;124mr ∈ {-1, 2} and c ≡ color mod 3 and c is within the range [-1, n-1] (roughly).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThis is a key insight! The 2×n strip can be reduced to 1 piece at a controlled [0m
