[38;2;124;124;124m**Direct proof of 2×n → 1:**[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe 2×n strip at rows 0-1, cols 0..n-1. I'll describe a construction that [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mreduces it to 1 piece.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mKey idea: Use the two rows as a "1D reduction with a buffer." The vertical jumps[0m[38;2;124;124;124mallow pieces to move between rows, creating holes that enable horizontal jumps.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe construction processes the strip from left to right in 3-column chunks. For [0m[38;2;124;124;124meach chunk, the zigzag pattern:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m1. Moves 2 pieces from the chunk to row 2 (below the strip).[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m2. Consolidates them in row 2 using a horizontal jump.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m3. Moves the consolidated piece back to row 0 or 1.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mAfter processing all chunks, the remaining pieces are in a 2×k block (k = n mod [0m[38;2;124;124;124m3, which is 1 or 2), which can be reduced to 1 (base case).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me work out the details for a single 3-column chunk.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Processing a 3-column chunk (cols j, j+1, j+2):**[0m

