[38;2;124;124;124mI was wrong earlier — the jump doesn't go over the square just outside the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mblock. It goes over a square INSIDE the block (0, 0) to a square OUTSIDE the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mblock (0, -1). The square just outside (0, -1) is the destination, not the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mjumped-over square.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo the first jumps in the (n+3)×(n+3) block are jumps from the edge of the block[0m[38;2;124;124;124mover an adjacent edge piece to a square just outside the block. For example:[0m
