[38;2;124;124;124mverify the full inductive step: (n+3)×(n+3) → n×n + 2 extra pieces, then → 1.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe key challenge is handling the remainders when n+3 is odd (1-row remainder [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mafter left absorption) or n is odd (1-column remainder after top absorption).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me think about this more carefully. The cases are:[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor n ≡ 1 mod 3: n = 1, 4, 7, 10, 13, ...[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- n=1: n+3=4 (even), n=1 (odd). Left absorption: 2 strips, no remainder. Top [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mabsorption: 0 2-col strips + 1 col remainder.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- n=4: n+3=7 (odd), n=4 (even). Left absorption: 3 strips + 1 row remainder. Top[0m[38;2;124;124;124mabsorption: 2 2-col strips, no remainder.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- n=7: n+3=10 (even), n=7 (odd). Left absorption: 5 strips, no remainder. Top [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mabsorption: 3 2-col strips + 1 col remainder.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- n=10: n+3=13 (odd), n=10 (even). Left absorption: 6 strips + 1 row remainder. [0m[38;2;124;124;124mTop absorption: 5 2-col strips, no remainder.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor n ≡ 2 mod 3: n = 2, 5, 8, 11, 14, ...[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- n=2: n+3=5 (odd), n=2 (even). Left absorption: 2 strips + 1 row remainder. Top[0m[38;2;124;124;124mabsorption: 1 2-col strip, no remainder.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- n=5: n+3=8 (even), n=5 (odd). Left absorption: 4 strips, no remainder. Top [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mabsorption: 2 2-col strips + 1 col remainder.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- n=8: n+3=11 (odd), n=8 (even). Left absorption: 5 strips + 1 row remainder. [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mTop absorption: 4 2-col strips, no remainder.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- n=11: n+3=14 (even), n=11 (odd). Left absorption: 7 strips, no remainder. Top [0m[38;2;124;124;124mabsorption: 5 2-col strips + 1 col remainder.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo the pattern is:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- When n is even: n+3 is odd, so left absorption has a 1-row remainder, but top [0m[38;2;124;124;124mabsorption has no remainder.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- When n is odd: n+3 is even, so left absorption has no remainder, but top [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mabsorption has a 1-column remainder.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor the case with a 1-row remainder (n even):[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mAfter left absorption: (n+2)×n block at rows 0..n+1, cols 3..n+2, plus 1×(n+3) [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mrow at row n+2, cols 0..n+2.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mThe 1×(n+3) row has 3 extra pieces at cols 0..2 (not covered by the block).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor the top absorption, I process 2-column strips. Each 2-column strip at cols [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m3+2k, 4+2k includes:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- (n+2)×2 from the block (rows 0..n+1)[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- 1×2 from the remainder row (row n+2)[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- Combined: (n+3)×2 strip[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe rotated absorption converts (n+3)×2 to n×2. ✓[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mAfter processing all n/2 2-column strips (n even), the result is:[0m
